# Protected core — these paths carry the security invariants. Changes should get a
# platform-owner review; feature work in src/routes/ and web/ deliberately does NOT.
#
# Today this is review-ROUTING, not a hard merge gate: GitHub branch protection is
# deliberately off (DECISIONS 2026-06-12), so the enforced gate is the PR convention +
# the guard-bash hook. CODEOWNERS only auto-requests review when the owner below is a
# collaborator on the repo — so in a FORKED app repo, repoint @yonico to that app's owner
# (ideally a CialDNB org TEAM, e.g. @CialDNB/<team>, which survives forking; none exists
# for this yet — see OPEN-QUESTIONS B4). Add a second owner to close the bus-factor (B4).
#
# Multi-person apps: see docs/COLLABORATION.md. A second person is the trigger to turn branch
# protection ON (require PR + CI + Code Owner review) — that's when CODEOWNERS becomes a real merge
# gate. Until then it stays advisory, so it never blocks a solo builder. To list two owners, put
# both on the line, e.g.:  /src/auth/   @owner-a @owner-b

# --- worker / framework / security-bearing source ---
/src/framework/         @yonico
/src/auth/              @yonico
/src/data/              @yonico
/src/email/             @yonico
/src/security/          @yonico
/src/ai/                @yonico
/src/cron/              @yonico
/src/mcp/               @yonico
/src/platform/          @yonico
/src/index.ts           @yonico
/src/health.ts          @yonico
/src/env.ts             @yonico
# The in-app agent's client (the AG-UI stream, the panel's reducer and state, the UI-intent
# allowlist) — it renders model output and turns it into navigation, so it is core like src/ai/,
# even though it lives under web/. The rest of web/ stays feature territory.
/web/src/agent/         @yonico

# --- schema, migrations, and the security headers (mirrored worker + SPA) ---
/schema.sql             @yonico
/migrations/            @yonico
/web/public/_headers    @yonico

# --- gates, harness, and build/config ---
/semgrep/               @yonico
/test/isolation/        @yonico
/test/helpers/          @yonico
# The test runtimes: the reviewed manifests that move a suite out of full Workers, the minimal
# Worker and its config, and the Node project's network guard (docs/TESTING.md).
/test/projects.mjs      @yonico
/test/runtime/          @yonico
/test/setup/            @yonico
/test/platform/source-hygiene.test.mjs @yonico
/.github/               @yonico
/.claude/               @yonico
/.githooks/             @yonico
/scripts/               @yonico
/wrangler.jsonc         @yonico
/wrangler.staging.jsonc @yonico
/wrangler.test.jsonc    @yonico
# The reviewed grant for private-database bindings. Cloudflare has no per-Worker scope for a
# Hyperdrive / Workers VPC binding, so this file IS the boundary — it and the wrangler configs
# above must move together, in one reviewed PR. See docs/DATA-ROUTES.md.
/binding-allowlist.jsonc @yonico
/tsconfig.json          @yonico
# All three typecheck configs (`npm run typecheck` runs each): loosening the test or SPA one
# weakens the gate exactly as loosening the worker's does.
/test/tsconfig.json     @yonico
/web/tsconfig.json      @yonico
/vitest.config.ts       @yonico
# The app's test-performance budget: the limits, job names and comparison files the CI
# observer reads. Raising a limit to quiet a sustained warning is a change to the evidence.
/test-performance-budget.json @yonico
/biome.json             @yonico

# --- agent guidance (the working agreement + its cross-tool mirrors + drift guard) ---
# CLAUDE.md is canonical; AGENTS.md symlinks to it; the Cursor rule + PLAYBOOKS are curated
# mirrors kept honest by verify:agents (docs/agent-guidance.sync.json). Edits here change how
# every builder — in any editor — is steered, so they carry a code-owner review.
/CLAUDE.md                      @yonico
/AGENTS.md                      @yonico
/.cursor/                       @yonico
/docs/PLAYBOOKS.md              @yonico
/docs/agent-guidance.sync.json  @yonico
